It is important to note that the criteria used to distinguish between exothermic and endothermic reactions can vary depending on the specific reaction and the conditions under which it occurs. Additionally, the energy released in exothermic reactions can be converted into other forms of energy, while the energy released in endothermic reactions cannot.
